WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.330
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:13.370
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for October 4th, on which we commemorate,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:20.270
St. Ammon, the Egyptian, who died in peace.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:24.990
Our Holy Father Ammon's parents died in his childhood.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:30.590
He was brought up by an uncle who made him marry when he was still very young.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:37.270
On the night of his wedding, as soon as he and his wife retired to the bridal chamber,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:43.830
Ammon took up the holy scriptures and read the passage in the epistle to the Corinthians

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:49.990
where the Apostle speaks of the disadvantages of marriage because of all the troubles and

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.630
cares that come with it.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:59.210
While virgins consecrated to the Lord can devote themselves without distraction to prayer

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:06.970
and to spiritual labor, both spouses took the following words literally.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:14.490
From now on, let those who have wives be as though they had none, and those who deal with

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.690
the world as though they had no dealings with it.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:25.690
They decided to remain in their virginity and to retire together to a desert place where

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:30.850
they could give themselves over to prayer and fasting.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:37.330
They set out for the mountain of nitria some way from Alexandria and settled in a little

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:45.810
hut there, but living together as man and woman, they soon realized the inexperience of tempting

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:51.570
nature head on and of provoking the attacks of demons.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:57.490
They parted company therefore each to live separately in Askeesies.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:06.890
Ammon never used wine or oil but lived only on dry bread that he ate every two or three days.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:12.090
His manner of life was pleasing to the Lord and a great many brethren who wanted to embrace

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.290
the monastic life soon came to join him.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:23.050
When a new aspirant arrived, Ammon would immediately let him have his own cell with everything

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:29.250
in it, and the other brethren would secretly bring provisions to the newcomer or whatever

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.090
else might be useful.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:40.090
This showed that fraternal love was first among the laws observed in this ever-growing brotherhood.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:46.650
In a few years under the direction of Ammon, the desert of nitria was transformed into a

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.770
veritable city.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.970
Some of the brethren now wanted to build their cells at a distance where they could live in

00:02:53.970 --> 00:03:01.850
greater solitude, so when one day Saint Antony the Great came to visit him, Abba Ammon asked

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:06.610
his advice about the place to choose.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:14.730
After taking a scanty meal together, they walked in the desert until sunset when they set

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:22.130
up across at the place they had reached so that those who wanted to could build their cells

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:25.690
there with the blessing of the two elders.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:34.850
In this way Abba Antony said, the brethren coming from nitria after a meal at the ninth hour

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:40.330
to see those who are here will meet them at this moment.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:47.570
And if those who leave here to go to nitria do the same, they will not lose their easy

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.930
hea, stillness.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:58.850
This was how the desert of Kellia, the cells, came to be established almost twelve miles from

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:08.210
nitria, more than 600 monks were soon living there, each in his own cell.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:15.290
Saint Ammon and Saint Antony were united in a deep spiritual friendship, when Abba Ammon

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:20.490
gave up his soul in peace to the Lord at nitria.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:27.570
Antony far away on his mountain broke off from the conversation he was having with some monks,

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:36.850
and in ecstasy saw the soul of Ammon going up to heaven accompanied by the joyful hymns

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:40.010
of a multitude of angels.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:45.770
Among other words inspired by the Holy Spirit, Saint Ammon said,

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:56.630
There with everyone as God bears with you through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:01.550
Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
